# OpenMed v1 — Requirements

## Objective

Develop a low-cost, portable, 2-channel biomedical signal acquisition
platform initially optimized for EMG research and signal analysis.

## Functional Requirements

FR-01: Acquire two differential EMG channels.
FR-02: Provide analog amplification appropriate for low-amplitude biosignals.
FR-03: Provide analog band-limiting before ADC conversion.
FR-04: Digitize acquired signals at a sufficient sampling rate for EMG.
FR-05: Transfer acquired data to a host computer.
FR-06: Support real-time digital signal processing.
FR-07: Calculate basic EMG features including RMS amplitude and signal envelope.
FR-08: Operate from battery power for portable use.

## Engineering Targets

Sampling rate: >= 2 kS/s/channel
Target EMG bandwidth: approximately 20–500 Hz
Channels: 2
PCB: 2-layer
Target prototype BOM: <$50–$100
Host interface: USB initially
Future interface: BLE
Future biosignals: ECG and PPG

## Validation

The system will be characterized using controlled electrical
test signals before any biological signal acquisition is attempted.

Measurements will include:

- Gain
- Frequency response
- Noise
- Input-referred noise
- Common-mode rejection
- ADC performance
- Sampling integrity
- Power consumption
